  "Question": "\\(\\left(\\dfrac14\\right)^{-\\frac{1}{4}}=\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-16\\)",
    "B": "\\(-\\sqrt2\\)",
    "C": "\\(-\\frac1{16}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\frac1{256}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\sqrt2\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "A negative exponent takes the reciprocal, and an exponent of \\(1/4\\) means the positive fourth root. Since the base is positive,\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac14\\right)^{-1/4}\n=4^{1/4}\n=\\sqrt{\\sqrt4}\n=\\boxed{\\sqrt2}.\n\\]\nThus the answer is choice E.",
